exports[`?cv=backend page text matches the reviewed copy 1`] = `"Skip to contentAboutExperienceSkillsEducationContactEridan WincklerBackend Engineer | Java 17/21, Spring Boot, REST APIs, ERP Integrations, Docker, AWSBrazil | Remote, UTC-3, overlaps US Eastern business hoursResumeLinkedInGitHubAbout MeBrazil-based backend engineer with four-plus years of professional Java and Spring Boot development (Jun 2022 to present) on a fully remote US team.Builds Java/Spring Boot services, including a Testcontainers-tested sync service feeding an AWS Bedrock knowledge base.Maintains REST API integrations between enterprise content management (ECM, ELO Digital Office) and ERP/SaaS platforms (Business Central, QuickBooks Online, SAP Business One, DocuSign).Builds the automation that provisions, deploys, and releases the platform (Ansible, Docker, GitLab CI/CD, AWS).Authored the CI/CD recommendation, adopted May 2026, moving the company from Jenkins to GitLab.Delivers customer projects end to end, from bare-VM install to production incident response.Documents for handover by default (65 Confluence pages, 22 decision records).Contact DetailsEridan WincklerBrazil, remote (UTC-3)efwinckler@gmail.comDownload ResumeLinkedInExperienceOvitas Inc.Burlington, MA, USA (fully remote)Software EngineerJun 2024 - PresentReplaced a ~50-step manual environment setup with a 13-role Ansible provisioning system (configuration management and Linux administration as code) that takes a bare AWS Linux VM to a working ECM and integration platform in a single run and ends with a ~60-check verification playbook; ships as a Docker image so operators need no local Ansible, Java, or Python. Rebuilt the deployment tool it runs into a modular, rerunnable phase orchestrator.Authored the CI/CD recommendation that set the company's migration from Jenkins to GitLab (adopted May 2026); registered the company's first GitLab runner and shipped its first three pipelines: environment configuration sync, sprint-boundary schema sync, and package build/publish with drift detection. Owned release engineering: Python release automation that generates Confluence release notes from Jira sprints, plus the version, documentation, and security-scan gates.Built a Java 17 / Spring Boot master-data sync service replicating SAP-fed SQL Server data to JSON for an AWS Bedrock knowledge base: read-only against the customer schema, verified crash recovery, ~8,000 rows/second measured, 34 Testcontainers integration tests.Sole-authored a one-command local platform stack (~11 Docker containers behind an Apache reverse proxy with TLS, up in ~25 minutes on a laptop), built to end contention for shared VPN-only dev VMs; its customer profiles reproduce a specific customer's environment with no code changes.Maintained and extended third-party REST API integrations with ERP/SaaS platforms: Dynamics 365 Business Central (OAuth2, OData incremental sync), QuickBooks Online, SAP Business One, DocuSign, and WordPress publishing.Junior Software EngineerJun 2022 - Jun 2024Eliminated a codebase-wide class of concurrency errors (ConcurrentModificationException from multi-threaded SDK connections in plugins) by designing a shared Java connection wrapper and refactoring 283 files across every module and plugin of a large multi-module Java platform.Replaced hand-run deployment steps with the platform's first Java deployment tool (ServiceManager, keystore generation and comparison, YAML generation with automatic backups; 83 files), still in use today as a phase of the Ansible provisioning system.Made Docker the standard deployment model for the Java integration services: containerized them and drove adoption, documented as a 14-page program.SkillsJavaSpring BootGitLab CI/CDLinuxDockerAnsibleAWSSQLAlso worked withProgramming LanguagesJava 21, Java 17, Python, JavaScript, TypeScript, Bash, SQLBackendSpring Boot, Spring WebFlux (WebClient), R2DBC, REST APIs, OAuth2, webhooks, OSGi plugins, Apache Tomcat, Maven, Gradle, microservicesDevOps & CI/CDAnsible (configuration management, infrastructure as code), GitLab CI/CD, Jenkins, Docker, Docker Compose, Git, YAML, configuration as code, Windows Server and Windows containersCloud & InfrastructureAWS (EC2, S3, CloudWatch, Lambda, Bedrock knowledge bases), Linux administration (Amazon Linux 2023, Ubuntu), Apache HTTP Server (reverse proxy), TLS/SSL, Certbot/Let's EncryptDatabases & SearchPostgreSQL, Microsoft SQL Server, MySQL, DynamoDB, ElasticsearchAI ToolingModel Context Protocol (MCP) server development, Claude Code custom commands, OpenAI APITesting, Process & DocsUnit tests and integration tests (JUnit, Testcontainers), mutation testing, Agile/Scrum, Jira, Confluence, MkDocs, secrets management (Jasypt, 1Password)Education & CertificationsEducationUninter InternationalB.S. in Software Engineering • 2019 - 2022Bachelor's degree covering software engineering principles and the full software development life cycle.Pontifícia Universidade Católica do Paraná (PUCPR)Law studies • 2008 - 2013CertificationsModel Context ProtocolAnthropic AcademyCompleted in Apr 2026Claude Code in ActionAnthropic AcademyCompleted in Apr 2026Building with the Claude APIAnthropic AcademyCompleted in Apr 2026Agent SkillsAnthropic AcademyCompleted in Mar 2026ContactThe best way to reach me is by email or on LinkedIn.Email meLinkedIn© 2026 Eridan Winckler"`;

